mrl-deskbook pack: content licence
====================================

This pack derived from:
Manufacturing Readiness Level (MRL) Deskbook
Version 2025
1 May 2025
(Includes Updates to MRL Criteria Matrix Effective 8 July 2025)
DOPSR Case # 25-T-1829.
Prepared by Office of the Secretary of Defense Manufacturing Technology
Program (OSD ManTech), in collaboration with the Joint Service/Industry
MRL Working Group.

Source licence: Public Domain (US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105); Distribution A,
approved public release; distribution unlimited. (tier 1; see ../../docs/SOURCE-VETTING.md)
No source-material download link published (see ../../docs/LICENSING.md).

This source work is a United States Government work, prepared by/for the Department
of Defense, and therefore NOT subject to copyright protection in the United States
(17 U.S.C. 105). It is marked Distribution A (approved public release; distribution
unlimited) and may be reproduced and distributed without permission.
The cover does not print a copyright notice.

ADVISORY-STATUS NOTICE (reproduced from source). The Deskbook's own page 2 states:

"This document is not a DoD requirement and is offered as a best practice."

Accordingly, this pack is advisory, not a mandate. Nothing in it overrides DoD policy,
statute, Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR), or Defense Federal Acquisition
Regulation Supplement (DFARS). MRL criteria are descriptive (they state what
maturity looks like) and do not, by themselves, task any contractor to perform work.

MATRIX AND WORKBOOK. Appendix A inside the pinned deskbook is the criteria matrix.
This pack does not reproduce it cell by cell. The Excel MRL Users Guide remains a
separate workbook. This pack describes its use and does not reproduce worksheet
cells.

Caveat: any DoD publication may incorporate third-party copyrighted images or material
whose separate reproduction could require permission of the copyright holder. This
pack reproduces no such third-party material. It contains only synthesized, transformed
reference notes. That caveat does not apply to this pack's content.

Attribution to OSD ManTech and the Joint Service/Industry MRL Working Group is provided
as a courtesy (see repository NOTICE), not as a legal obligation. The Working Group
does not endorse this pack or its authors.

